# Commit code changes

When you change files in this repository, commit those changes before finishing the task.

- Commit on the `cursor` branch. Never commit to `main`.
- Stage the changes from the task. Leave unrelated files and secrets unstaged.
- Use a short imperative commit title with no trailing period, and usually no body.
- Do not push, force-push, tag, or release unless the user asks.
- If a hook fails, fix the problem and create a new commit.
- If there is nothing to commit, do not create an empty commit.

